    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, can you help me write a rejection email? I have a candidate who made it all the way to the final round for a software engineer role but we decided to go with someone else. I want it to sound professional but also empathetic so they don't feel bad about getting so far. Thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Hello there! I'd be happy to help you craft that rejection email. It is a delicate task, but if you can keep the tone firm yet kind, it will go well.\n\nHere is a draft you can use, which I have carefully reviewed for its professional tone and empathetic message.\n\n***\n\n**Subject:** Update Regarding Your Application for [Job Title]\n\nDear [Candidate Name],\n\nThank you for taking the time to interview for the Software Engineer position at [Company Name]. We were truly impressed by your technical skills and the depth of your experience during our conversations.\n\nAfter careful consideration by our team, we have decided to move forward with another candidate whose background aligns slightly more closely with our current project roadmap. This was not an easy decision, as we genuinely enjoyed getting to know you and believe you have great potential.\n\nWe hope you understand that this decision is not a reflection of your abilities, but rather a result of the specific needs of our team at this moment. We wish you the very best in your job search and hope our paths cross again in the future.\n\nSincerely,\n\n[Your Name]\n[Your Title]\n\n***\n\n**A few notes on this draft:**\n*   **",
      "source": "target",
